							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: September 08, 2005, 03:37:49 pm
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Ummmm, August 28th, 10am, MANDATORY Evac was called. Hell, I was watching CNN when that order came in. <br /><br />As for the levies, of course there wasn&#039;t enough time to build them up enough before the storm hit, should of been done over the years. BUT, it was known that the storm was gonna hit, and be a big nasty when it did. Stuff could of been in place for the Aftermath. Whenever a hurricane hits Florida, stuff is in place and ready to go. Why should Louisiana be any different? They are a part of the US if I recall. What most people have been saying is simple. An event of this magnitude needs more than state help, it needs Federal as well. Bush jumps whenever Florida needs him, he should do the same for any other state as well. Maybe if he had a family member running Louisiana he would of had help there sooner................Nuff said.</td>
